DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These convenience functions are used to retrieve and update class-depen‐
     dent _E_l_f_3_2___D_y_n or _E_l_f_6_4___D_y_n information in the ddyynnaammiicc table of an ELF
     object.

     Argument _d_a_t_a is an _E_l_f___D_a_t_a descriptor associated with a section of type
     SHT_DYNAMIC.  Argument _n_d_x is the index of the entry being retrieved or
     updated.  The class-independent _G_E_l_f___D_y_n structure is described in
     gelf(3).

     Function ggeellff__ggeettddyynn() retrieves the class-dependent entry at index _n_d_x
     in data buffer _d_a_t_a and copies it to the destination pointed to by argu‐
     ment _d_y_n after translation to class-independent form.

     Function ggeellff__uuppddaattee__ddyynn() converts the class-independent entry pointed
     to by argument _d_y_n to class-dependent form, and writes it to the entry at
     index _n_d_x in the data buffer described by argument _d_a_t_a.  Function
     ggeellff__uuppddaattee__ddyynn() signals an error if any of the values in the class-in‐
     dependent representation exceeds the representable limits of the target
     type.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     Function ggeellff__ggeettddyynn() returns the value of argument _d_y_n if successful,
     or NULL in case of an error.  Function ggeellff__uuppddaattee__ddyynn() returns a non-
     zero value if successful, or zero in case of an error.

